# Wrangler credentials for deploying the Cloudflare-hosted MemPalace Worker.
#
# Setup:
#   cp .env.example .env
#   Fill in both values. .env is gitignored; never commit it.
#
# Wrangler reads these from .env in the project root for every command
# (deploy, d1, vectorize, r2, secret). You can skip this file and use
# `npx wrangler login` instead, which stores an OAuth session in your home
# directory.
#
# This file is for deploying only. MEMPALACE_API_KEY does not go here:
#   - On the Worker, it is a secret: npx wrangler secret put MEMPALACE_API_KEY
#   - On each client machine, export it in your shell profile so Cursor's
#     mcp.json can read it as ${env:MEMPALACE_API_KEY}.

# Create at https://dash.cloudflare.com/profile/api-tokens with "Start from
# scratch" and these Account permissions, scoped to your account only:
#   Workers Scripts: Edit
#   Workers AI: Edit
#   Vectorize: Edit
#   D1: Edit
#   Workers R2 Storage: Edit
#   Account Settings: Read
CLOUDFLARE_API_TOKEN=

# Shown on the right side of the dashboard's Workers & Pages overview page,
# or run: npx wrangler whoami
CLOUDFLARE_ACCOUNT_ID=

# Note: during `npx wrangler dev`, Wrangler also loads .env into the local
# Worker's env. If you create a .dev.vars file, Wrangler loads that instead
# of .env. Put a local-only MEMPALACE_API_KEY in .dev.vars, not here.
